ORC-VAL6TMKMVK,GE-SE,TRANSITION_TEMPERATURE,phase transition,,running_text,931.4,K,,,,10.0,10.0,model_calculated,931.4,931.4 K,101325,βGeSe,,,,model,,true,doi:10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,"Shanxiong Chen, Jiong Wang, Shangzhao Yu, Biao Hu, Qing Wu, Yong Du, Thermodynamic Modeling of the Ge-X (X = As, Se, S, P) Systems, J. Electron. Mater. 51, 2114-2130 (2022).",p. 10,10,"In the present thermodynamic assessment, the melting point of ␀GeS2 is 1110 K, βGeSe melts incongruently at 931.4 K, and the transition between αGeS and βGeS occurs at"
ORC-YXHHCPEWAH.89f45b,GE-SE,INVARIANT_TEMPERATURE,invariant reaction,,running_text,851.0,K,,,,5.0,5.0,thermal_analysis,851.0,851 K,101325,,eutectic,Liquid#2 → GeSe + ␀GeSe2,,experimental,thermal analysis,false,doi:10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,"Shanxiong Chen, Jiong Wang, Shangzhao Yu, Biao Hu, Qing Wu, Yong Du, Thermodynamic Modeling of the Ge-X (X = As, Se, S, P) Systems, J. Electron. Mater. 51, 2114-2130 (2022).",p. 5,5,"They discovered a monotectic reaction, Liquid#1 → Liquid#2 + (Ge) at 1173 K; a peritectic reaction, Liquid#2 + (Ge) → GeSe at 934 K; and an eutectic reaction, Liquid#2 → GeSe + ␀GeSe2 at 851 K."
ORC-YXHHCPEWAH.eff00c,GE-SE,INVARIANT_TEMPERATURE,invariant reaction,,running_text,934.0,K,,,,5.0,5.0,thermal_analysis,934.0,934 K,101325,,peritectic,Liquid#2 + (Ge) → GeSe,,experimental,thermal analysis,false,doi:10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,"Shanxiong Chen, Jiong Wang, Shangzhao Yu, Biao Hu, Qing Wu, Yong Du, Thermodynamic Modeling of the Ge-X (X = As, Se, S, P) Systems, J. Electron. Mater. 51, 2114-2130 (2022).",p. 5,5,"They discovered a monotectic reaction, Liquid#1 → Liquid#2 + (Ge) at 1173 K; a peritectic reaction, Liquid#2 + (Ge) → GeSe at 934 K; and an eutectic reaction, Liquid#2 → GeSe + ␀GeSe2 at 851 K."
ORC-L5FOQ6ASVN,GE-SE,TRANSITION_TEMPERATURE,phase transition,,running_text,1013.15,K,,,,5.0,5.0,thermal_analysis,1013.15,1013.15 K,101325,GeSe2,congruent transformation,,,experimental,thermal analysis,true,doi:10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,10.1007/s11664-022-09474-1,"Shanxiong Chen, Jiong Wang, Shangzhao Yu, Biao Hu, Qing Wu, Yong Du, Thermodynamic Modeling of the Ge-X (X = As, Se, S, P) Systems, J. Electron. Mater. 51, 2114-2130 (2022).",p. 5,5,"Meanwhile, the ␀GeSe2 phase melting congruently at 1013.15 K was also confirmed."
